From 1714d837ba5af273d082d6a48d85e392bda93d71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GrgaPalcic <26028466+GrgaPalcic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:27:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: a disk recall's home is the part of the prefix the
 tree holds; a kept state whose home is not its pages' part is not resumed

A recall filed its state under the part with fewer live streams while its resume adopted the tree's pages of the
prefix, in the other part. The resume then carried latent rows between the ranks, and for a state past the shared
store's pages the two sides cut that carry apart: the sender had nothing to send, the receiver waited for every row,
and a two-Spark pair running this stack hung (2026-11-11, 7 h).

- Image.blank_pages takes `near`, a page the tree holds of the prompt; Store.recall passes firstHeld(prompt) and
  GLM's blankPages takes its part as the home when it has the room.
- cuda_share.begin: a pending state whose home is not its adopted pages' part is evicted and the pass runs cold.
- cuda_snapshots.restore: a carry for a state with shared pages is error.KvShardNotHome on every rank, before any
  NCCL call.
- Host tests: begin with a state at home in its pages' part resumes, with the other home it does not.
